{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775327603-Ctqwn7RaUM31DLn2wJeu","role":"assistant","created":1775327622,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see from the tables that there's \"Social Security Administration\" row with budget outlays. Let me look at more data from the other years. I need to understand what data I need:\n\n1. From each December Treasury Bulletin (odd years: 2011, 2013, 2015, 2017, 2019), I need to extract the Social Security Administration nominal budget outlay from the FFO-4 tables.\n\n2. These tables show \"This fiscal year to date\" and \"Prior fiscal year to date\" - I need the \"This fiscal year to date\" which should represent the full fiscal year outlay.\n\nLet me look at each file to get the Social Security Administration total funds (column 4) for \"This fiscal year to date\":\n\nFrom 2011 (page 25): Social Security Administration - Total funds = 784,194 (this fiscal year to date)\nThis is for FY2011, which represents FY2011 data.\n\nBut wait, I need to think about this more carefully. The task asks for FY2010 to FY2019. Looking at the December bulletins:\n- December 2011 table would show FY2011 (current) and FY2010 (prior)\n- December 2013 table would show FY2013 (current) and FY2012 (prior)\n- December 2015 table would show FY2015 (current) and FY2014 (prior)\n- December 2017 table would show FY2017 (current) and FY2016 (prior)\n- December 2019 table would show FY2019 (current) and FY2018 (prior)\n\nSo from these bulletins I can get data for:\n- FY2011 from 2011 bulletin (this fiscal year)\n- FY2013 from 2013 bulletin (this fiscal year)\n- FY2015 from 2015 bulletin (this fiscal year)\n- FY2017 from 2017 bulletin (this fiscal year)\n\n\n- FY2019 from 2019 bulletin (this fiscal year)\n\nI realize the task specifically requires using odd years between 2010 and 2019, which means I'll need to carefully map the available fiscal year data to this requirement.\n\nThe December bulletins provide an interesting solution: they contain the current fiscal year's data alongside the prior year's data. This means I can extract the needed information by cross-referencing the bulletins from different years.\n\nMy strategy will involve using the December 2011 bulletin to access FY2010 data and the December 2019 bulletin to retrieve FY2019 data. This approach should give me the comprehensive dataset I need for the specified time range.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_446b094049fb75f6","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2015_12_page_23.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
