ed.\n\nI'll extract the total funds for Social Security Administration from each table:\n- 2011: 784,194\n- 2013: 867,394\n- 2015: 944,143\n- 2017: 1,000,812\n- 2019: 1,101,833\n\nThese values are in millions of dollars, representing the total funds for each fiscal year. I'll proceed with calculating the coefficient of variation using these data points.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_5e6b04ccc1cd8254","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# Data values (in millions)\nvalues = [784194, 867394, 944143, 1000812, 1101833]\n\n# Calculate mean\nn = len(values)\nmean = sum(values) / n\n\n# Calculate population variance and population standard deviation\n# Population std dev = sqrt(sum((x - mean)^2) / n)\nsum_squared_diff = sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in values)\npop_variance = sum_squared_diff / n\npop_std_dev = math.sqrt(pop_variance)\n\n# Calculate coefficient of variation\ncv = (pop_std_dev / mean) * 100\n\nprint(f\"Values: {values}\")\nprint(f\"N: {n}\")\nprint(f\"Mean: {mean:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Population Variance: {pop_variance:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Population Std Dev: {pop_std_dev:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Coefficient of Variation: {cv:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to nearest hundredths: {round(cv, 2)}%\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
